{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nBefore any change-size/decomposition rule can enter the DET floor, measure whether change shape actually drives the defect-rework loop here (11-plan-v3 I-4; measurement-first matches the field — Prow's `size/*` labels are non-blocking, 12c). Tooling anchor (12a): extend `scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py` (442 lines), which imports the shipped predicate `BUGFIX_SIZE_THRESHOLD_NON_TEST_LINES` and `escalation_for_diff` from `rebar.llm.code_review.bugfix_size_gate` so its threshold cannot drift from the gate that ships. 2026 grounding (12b): MSR'26 agentic-PR studies show files-touched/commit fragmentation is a sharper variable than raw LOC, the size-quality relationship is nonstationary (re-tune, never freeze), and context fragmentation is an independent causal variable (39% quality drop in a controlled study). The two doubling friction categories (CI-at-landing 25/60; environment 13/60 — R2S3) are unexplained and get mechanism reads, not guesses.\n\n## Approach\n\n**Step 0 — overlap check, before building.** 11-plan-v3 I-4 requires confirming this does not duplicate the Tier-2 replay harness (ADR 0109, `1299d9deb6da`, `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/`). The finding is recorded in the backtest report's Method section either way; if the harness already supplies a variable, this task consumes it rather than re-deriving it.\n\n**Read (a) — change shape.** Extend the backtest with an all-work mode (not just bug-typed tickets) measuring rework against three variables: non-test LOC (via the already-imported `count_non_test_diff_lines`), files touched (`git show --name-only`), and commit fragmentation (commits per ticket, grouped by the `rebar-ticket:` trailer). The script computes no correlation today — only a recall summary — so this adds a statistical layer rather than extending one. Rework signals, in order of cost: ticket-level proxies already shipped in `rebar metrics` (`attempts_per_ticket`, `revert_recovery`, `reopen_recovery`, `first_pass_rate`); store `caused_by` fan-in, which is the same label source the script already uses; and patchset count from Gerrit `o=ALL_REVISIONS`, which is the cheapest per-change rework proxy and the only one requiring the network.\n\n**The join key, explicitly.** Shape is measured PER COMMIT; rework is measured PER TICKET, so the two are aligned on the **full canonical rebar ticket id** taken from each commit's FIRST `rebar-ticket:` trailer (parsed with the shipped `extract_ticket_refs`). Commits fold into tickets with `group_by_ticket`, which SUMS the per-commit shape variables into per-ticket aggregates (non-test LOC, total LOC, commit count) and unions files-touched; the resulting per-ticket row is what correlates against the per-ticket rework signals. A commit whose trailer does not resolve to exactly one full canonical id in the store — an ambiguous 4-quad fragment, or a ticket no longer present — is UNJOINABLE: it is excluded from the correlation and its count is reported, never silently dropped. This is also why the window starts 2026-07-01: trailer coverage on `origin/main` is 60/650 in June (pre-enforcement, unjoinable) against 876/907 in July.\n\n**Read (b) — CI-at-landing.** The doubling window is 2026-08-25..2026-08-30 (the newer-30 half of R2S3's 60 session logs). No case list is committed, so the 20 cases are derived: session-log mining over that window for `Verified -1` / CI-failure patterns, cross-referenced to the specific Gerrit changes R2S3 already names. Each case is read for mechanism, change shape, cross-session interference, isolation class, and drift class.\n\n**Read (c) — environment.** Session reports are `session_log` tickets, queryable offline via `rebar session-logs -o json`. The automated `llm-degrade NEEDS_INVESTIGATION` logs carry a structured JSON body (`exception_type`, `message`, `model`) and are countable without keyword heuristics; the remainder are read for mechanism. Output projects specific fields — a full dump is dominated by authorship ledgers and is unusably large.\n\n**Decision.** The size/decomposition enforcement decision is recorded either way as ADR 0110 (next free number; `docs/adr/.numbers/0110` marker committed alongside, which is the race-free uniqueness mechanism). `docs/adr/README.md` is GENERATED by `scripts/gen_adr_index.py` and must be regenerated, never hand-edited.\n\n**Dependency.** `reports/` is gitignored; the `.gitignore` re-inclusion of `reports/stability/` lands in sibling `yogic-soapstone-takin` (f9b9-83ad-931c-4833), which sits below this change in the stack. This task inherits it and adds no second `.gitignore` edit.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] AC1: `reports/stability/change-shape-backtest.md` is committed, giving the distribution of all three variables (non-test LOC, files touched, commit fragmentation) and each one's measured relationship to rework, with n stated inline. Verified by `git ls-files reports/stability/change-shape-backtest.md`.\n- [x] AC2: read (a) is reproducible — the report's Method section names the exact command, and re-running it reproduces the reported n. Verified by running the documented `python scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py ...` invocation.\n- [x] AC3: `reports/stability/ci-landing-regressions-read.md` is committed with a 20-row per-case table (mechanism, change shape, class) and states how the cases were selected from the 2026-08-25..2026-08-30 window.\n- [x] AC4: `reports/stability/environment-failures-read.md` is committed with per-case mechanisms and a class disposition per case, naming which dispositions feed the doctor-checks scope.\n- [x] AC5: the enforcement decision is recorded either way as `docs/adr/0110-*.md` with its supporting evidence, and `docs/adr/.numbers/0110` is committed. Verified by `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check` exiting 0 and `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` confirming the bijection.\n- [x] AC6: the Step-0 overlap finding against ADR 0109's replay harness is stated in the backtest report, so a later reader knows the boundary was checked.\n- [x] AC7: the extended script still imports the shipped threshold predicate rather than re-deriving it, so the backtest cannot drift from the gate. Verified by the existing import remaining, exercised by the script's tests.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `python scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py --check-planning-corpus` — the existing pinned-corpus self-check still passes, proving the all-work extension did not perturb the shipped bug-corpus path (AC7).\n- the documented all-work invocation from the report's Method section — re-runs read (a) and reproduces its n (AC2).\n- `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check` and `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` — the ADR is indexed and its number is uniquely claimed (AC5).\n- `git ls-files reports/stability/` — the three reports are tracked (AC1, AC3, AC4).\n- `make lint && make typecheck` — the script extension clears the house gates, including the complexity ratchet.\n\nMeasurement reads are evidence documents, not executable behavior, so their oracle is reproducibility (AC2) rather than a new automated test; the script change itself is covered by the pinned-corpus check above.\n\n## File impact\n\n- `scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py` (extend: all-work mode + files-touched/fragmentation variables and the correlation layer)\n- `reports/stability/change-shape-backtest.md` (new)\n- `reports/stability/ci-landing-regressions-read.md` (new)\n- `reports/stability/environment-failures-read.md` (new)\n- `docs/adr/0110-<slug>.md` and `docs/adr/.numbers/0110` (new; the enforcement decision)\n- `docs/adr/README.md` (regenerated by `scripts/gen_adr_index.py`)"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788344908164597001,"uuid":"f5127f9f-5c7b-4ebe-bafe-77a971b91bf6"}